# Change context: tighten-sdd-artifact-boundaries

## Current continuation — plan composition guidance (2026-10-26)

The owner requested a minimal executable plan structure and composition
recommendations in instructions. Detail follows the migration gap, rather than
the small/large category: resolved new development or a small feature may need
only ordered modules, code locations/names and architecture/validation links;
substantial existing-code/API migration needs explicit reuse/adaptation/removal/
replacement/new work, callers and transition order. This also covers refactoring
that preserves external behavior.

`schemas/sdd/templates/plan.md` now contains only the existing title and one
numbered checkbox placeholder. The schema plan instruction owns the conditional
composition guidance; optional shared notes/sections serve concrete execution
needs. Coverage can follow coherent architecture/validation references, with a
separate mapping only when useful to expose a gap. Permanent contracts/checks
retain their owners. Checkbox-only execution edits and all mechanical plan
contracts remain unchanged. The system delta's Plan row points to these
instructions, and approved-plan guidance is attributed to schema/skills rather
than the removed template boilerplate. Existing skills already load the schema
instructions; no skill-tree rewrite was needed.

Manager `/root/final_implementation_manager` provided bounded read-only guidance.
Root completed schema validation (six artifacts/five steps), actual emitted plan
instruction/template inspection, merged system preview, mechanical-contract
comparison, and diff checks. Evidence and exact current source hashes:
`../../probes/tighten-boundaries/plan-guidance/observations.json` and `review.patch`.
Both rules documents and the approved change plan (including completion marks)
are unchanged by this follow-up. No client/model probe, installer or commit ran.

The former p8 installed-schema identity no longer describes the changed schema
and template. Prior coordination evidence remains reusable only for unchanged
orchestration contracts; this source check claims no new model behavior or
current bootstrap installation. Live lifecycle remains `designing` with current
owner review pending from the earlier correction. New source edits/self-review
supply no artifact acceptance, structural revalidation or lifecycle advance.
The earlier records below describe their respective prior revisions.

