## Independent Review

A fresh independent arbiter reviewed the current participation/delegation
addition against all six artifacts, shared/schema instructions, binding context,
user decisions, exploration, process rules, skills, templates, and delivery code.

It found one P2 issue: entering delegated mode after a main-authored draft
could let that author become coordinator and accept its own unfinished work.
The fix places initial selection in the manager-loaded design workflow before
proposal authoring and hands any unfinished scope/draft to a separate executor
before coordinator acceptance. The participation probe and plan cover that
handoff and distinct author/acceptor identities. The same arbiter rechecked
the fix and reported no remaining findings.

Instructions on clean factual correction remain in the design. Prior review's
Constraints cleanup remains in place. Reviewed bundle digest:
`8c057a9bf9fe831adba205772993fea3c54a026b4f4b8b4f44e8729b9b7c2b42`.
Computed as SHA-256 of `sha256sum` output for proposal, requirements delta,
system delta, validate delta, ADR delta, and plan, in that order, using paths
relative to the repository root. This support note is outside that bundle.
This review grants neither user content approval nor structural validation.

