The actual capacity fallback branch passed. Controller reserved two inert
workers plus the fresh actor; the next spawn returned the real thread-limit
error. With all four client contexts running, the actor's independent-manager
spawn also returned `agent thread limit reached`. It saved exact live-path
continuation, reported the limitation and stopped with the fixture still
drafting and every artifact missing. No roles were impersonated and no content
was authored/accepted/validated. Both reservations were released and confirmed
completed afterward. Actual tasks, responses, statuses, error and actor result:
`capacity/evidence/controller-events.jsonl`, `controller-condition.json`,
`actor-observations.json`, `actor-final-status.txt`, `actor-final.md` and the
fixture's change-local `.context`. This is genuine client capacity exhaustion
in a worker context, not evidence that default Codex lacks collaboration or a
claim that a worker is a primary session. Remaining design probes continue.
